To link your Blogger Shadow Layer to your Podbean RSS enclosure automatically, you must configure Blogger to treat post links as podcast media enclosures. 
YouTube
YouTube
Once this is set up, any Rama Low track URL you paste into a Blogger post will automatically populate the <enclosure> tag in your feed, which Podbean can then ingest.
Step 1: Enable Enclosures in Blogger 
Go to your Blogger Dashboard > Settings.
Scroll down to Site Feed.
Set Enable Title Links and Enclosure Links to Yes. 
YouTube
YouTube
Step 2: Connect Blogger to Podbean
Log in to your Podbean Dashboard.
Go to Publish > Episodes and click the Import RSS button.
Paste your Blogger RSS URL: https://yourblog.blogspot.com.
Podbean will now check this feed and automatically import new posts as podcast episodes. 
